## notes (written after the run)
- the 'exit=' lines are the exit code of the grep filter in the stack script, not of the probe; the probe's verdict is its 'RESULT' line (exit 0 only on PASS). All 4 runs: RESULT PASS.
- good_key: 10 storage spans per run, all outcome=ok, all inside a traced request, all carrying a task_id; 4 rows in public.tasks = 2 runs x (1 chat + 1 task), i.e. the writes really reached PostgreSQL. http_status is recorded on failures only (the store passes no status on success).
- bad_key (service JWT altered): PostgREST rejects every write with 401; every storage span = fail/401; the API still answers 200 with persisted reported by the existing contract (unchanged).
- classification: LOCAL integration (loopback, throwaway JWT secret). Not live: no cloud Supabase, no paid LLM.
